        {
          "text": "\"ClosureBench: A Constructive Benchmark for Compositional Graph Reasoning\" proposes Learn more × License: CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 arXiv:2608.18242v1 [cs.LG] 18 Aug 2026 ClosureBench: A Constructive Benchmark for Compositional Graph Reasoning \\name Stefano Goria \\email stefano@aimresearchlab.com Affiliation: \\addr AIM Research Lab Affiliation: aimresearchlab.com Abstract",
          "evidence_class": "AUTHOR_CLAIM",
          "context": "Method/system claim as reported by the authors in the inspected body; not independently reproduced."
        },
        {
          "text": "Evaluation as reported: Tracking it is itself hard: new models are trained on the benchmarks used to evaluate them, so a fixed test set decays into a memorisation check soon after release, which has motivated constructive benchmarks that generate fresh instances on demand.",
          "evidence_class": "AUTHOR_CLAIM",
          "context": "Evaluation design/benchmark scope as described by the authors; benchmark choice and protocol not independently audited."
        },
        {
          "text": "Maker-reported result (not a publication-grade fact): Figure 2 plots the two curves: seen accuracy climbs to 78.5% while held-out plateaus at ∼ {\\sim} 59% after epoch 5, a 19.3pp gap.",
          "evidence_class": "AUTHOR_CLAIM",
          "context": "Author-reported numbers only; no independent reproduction or significance testing in captured bytes."
        },
        {
          "text": "The inspected body references a public code/model artifact location (repository or model-hub link present in body text).",
          "evidence_class": "PRIMARY_FACT",
          "context": "Artifact-link presence observed in body; availability/version not fetch-verified."
        }
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "All performance figures are maker-reported author claims from the paper body; no independent reproduction, significance test, or held-out audit exists in captured bytes.",
        "The inspected arXiv HTML full text exposes no dedicated limitations discussion captured by section parsing; absence-of-limitations is a parsing observation, not a quality judgment."
      ],
      "verification": [
        {
          "target": "Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.18242) in lane evaluation. Discovery triage only: matched=evaluation,language_models,training_methods; title_matches=evaluation,training_methods; score=9. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Large language models fail on multi-step compositional reasoning, but measuring that failure is hard, because new models are trained on the benchmarks used to evaluate them. A fixed test set becomes a memorisation check soon after release. Constructive benchmarks avoid this by generating instances on demand. We introduce ClosureBench, a constructive benchmark for graph-relational logical reasoning. Each task is built from explicit primitives (reachability, degree, set operations, connectivity, aggregation), and its reference answer is computed by executing code that implements that logic exact",
